{"hash":"f0417a31e4c473db","voice":"en-IN-NeerjaExpressiveNeural","rate":"+4%","dur":69.178,"said":"These tiers face the temple for a reason. Every evening, outside the monsoon, people fill them for the light and sound show, and as the lights come up on the temple walls, a voice begins. In this telling the storyteller is not a king or a priest, but the ocean itself, the sea behind you, which has watched this shore longer than anyone. It tells of Soma, the Moon, who did penance here and was healed by Shiva. It tells of the temple’s splendour, of the raids that broke it, and of the hands that raised it each time. It tells of Krishna’s last journey from Prabhasa, and of the brave Hamirji Gohil and Vegadaji Bhil. Ragas and chants rise and fall with the stories. Many visitors say the narration is in the famous voice of Amitabh Bachchan. The temple trust gives its time as eight to nine in the evening, but check at the counter, because rain and festivals can change it. Sit for a moment, and let the waves keep time.\n\nDid you know? In the show’s script the narrator is not a person at all, but the Arabian Sea.","segments":[{"key":"text","start":0,"end":923},{"key":"didYouKnow","start":939,"end":1017}],"words":[[0.098,0.349,0,5],[0.459,0.385,6,11],[0.855,0.288,12,16],[1.156,0.12,17,20],[1.288,0.445,21,27],[1.745,0.18,28,31],[1.937,0.048,32,33],[1.997,0.517,34,40],[3.365,0.421,42,47],[3.798,0.469,48,55],[4.447,0.541,57,64],[5.0,0.084,65,68],[5.096,0.685,69,76],[6.034,0.3,78,84],[6.346,0.252,85,89],[6.611,0.204,90,94],[6.827,0.12,95,98],[6.959,0.06,99,102],[7.031,0.421,103,108],[7.464,0.156,109,112],[7.632,0.325,113,118],[7.969,0.325,119,123],[8.558,0.168,125,128],[8.738,0.204,129,131],[8.954,0.096,132,135],[9.062,0.361,136,142],[9.435,0.204,143,147],[9.651,0.168,148,150],[9.832,0.132,151,153],[9.976,0.084,154,157],[10.072,0.421,158,164],[10.505,0.421,165,170],[11.118,0.132,172,173],[11.262,0.373,174,179],[11.647,0.529,180,186],[13.065,0.144,188,190],[13.221,0.216,191,195],[13